<title>BELGIUM: Benelux summit set for Friday, Saturday in Dublin.</title>
<headline>Benelux summit set for Friday, Saturday in Dublin.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The leaders of Belgium, the Netherlands and Luxembourg will hold their traditional pre-European Union summit meeting on Friday and Saturday in Dublin, the Belgian Foreign Ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The meeting between the three heads of government will begin at 1700 GMT on Friday and pick up at 0700 GMT on Saturday morning, the ministry said.</p>
<p>EU leaders are meeting for an informal summit on the bloc's future -- particularly the progress of the inter-governmental conference (IGC) -- on Saturday.</p>
<p>Benelux leaders usually meet before such summits to seek common ground for the regional bloc.</p>
</text>
